/**
\page devs_jobprocessor JobProcessor DEVS atomic model

\tableofcontents

\section jobprocessor_overview Overview

Single-server processor without a queue. It accepts one job on `in` while
`passive`, holds in `busy` for a fixed processing time, emits the job on `out`
and returns to `passive`. Jobs arriving while busy are dropped.

| | |
|---|---|
| Kind | Atomic DEVS model |
| Formalism | Parallel DEVS (PythonPDEVS) |
| Language / framework | Python / PythonPDEVS (pypdevs) |
| Source | `gen_proc.py` ( \ref gen_proc.JobProcessor ) |
| Parameters | `name` (default `"proc"`), `processing_time` (default 1.0) |
| Initial state | phase `passive`, sigma = INFINITY, job = None, processed = 0 |

\section jobprocessor_formal Formal specification

    M = < X, Y, S, delta_int, delta_ext, delta_con, lambda, ta >

- X = { (p, v) : p in InPorts, v in X_p } with InPorts = { in }
- Y = { (p, v) : p in OutPorts, v in Y_p } with OutPorts = { out }
- S = { passive, busy } x R0+ (sigma) x (Job or None) x N (processed)
- ta, delta_int, delta_ext, delta_con and lambda are tabulated in the sections below.

\section jobprocessor_ports Ports

\subsection jobprocessor_inports Input ports

| Port | Value type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `in` | `Job` | job to be processed; only the first value of the bag is taken |

\subsection jobprocessor_outports Output ports

| Port | Value type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `out` | `Job` | the finished job |

\section jobprocessor_state State

\subsection jobprocessor_phases Phases

| Phase | ta(s) | Meaning |
|---|---|---|
| `passive` | inf | idle, waiting for a job |
| `busy` | processing_time | serving the current job |

\subsection jobprocessor_vars State variables

| Variable | Type | Initial value | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `phase` | `str` | `"passive"` | discrete phase |
| `sigma` | `float` | `INFINITY` | remaining hold time |
| `job` | `Job` | `None` | job being served |
| `processed` | `int` | 0 | completed-job counter |

The variables are held in \ref gen_proc.ProcessorState "ProcessorState".

\section jobprocessor_ta Time advance ta(s)

`ta(s) = sigma`: `processing_time` while busy, `INFINITY` while passive.

\section jobprocessor_dint Internal transition delta_int(s)

| From phase | To phase | Action |
|---|---|---|
| `busy` | `passive` | processed += 1; job = None; sigma = INFINITY |

\section jobprocessor_dext External transition delta_ext(s, e, x)

| From phase | Port | Condition | To phase | Action |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| `passive` | `in` | at least one job in the bag | `busy` | job = first job; sigma = processing_time |
| `busy` | `in` | any | `busy` | sigma -= e; arriving jobs are dropped |

In PythonPDEVS the elapsed time e is `self.elapsed` inside `extTransition`.

\section jobprocessor_dcon Confluent transition delta_con(s, x)

Overridden: delta_int first, then delta_ext with `self.elapsed = 0.0`. A job
that arrives exactly when the current job completes is accepted immediately.

\section jobprocessor_lambda Output function lambda(s)

| Phase | Port | Value |
|---|---|---|
| `busy` | `out` | the current job |

\section jobprocessor_diagram State diagram

Solid edges are internal transitions (fired when ta(s) expires); dashed edges
are external transitions (fired on input). Labels use `trigger / action`.

\dot
digraph jobprocessor_states {
    rankdir=LR;
    node [shape=ellipse, fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=10];
    edge [fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=9];
    __init [shape=point];
    passive [label="passive\n(ta = inf)"];
    busy [label="busy\n(ta = processing_time)"];
    __init -> passive;
    busy -> passive [label="int / emit job, processed += 1"];
    passive -> busy [label="ext: in / job = first job", style=dashed];
    busy -> busy [label="ext: in / drop, sigma -= e", style=dashed];
}
\enddot

\section jobprocessor_source Source mapping

| DEVS element | Implementation in `gen_proc.py` |
|---|---|
| Ports | \ref gen_proc.JobProcessor.inport "JobProcessor.inport" (`"in"`), \ref gen_proc.JobProcessor.outport "JobProcessor.outport" (`"out"`) |
| State | \ref gen_proc.ProcessorState "ProcessorState" held in `JobProcessor.state` |
| Initialization | \ref gen_proc.JobProcessor.__init__ "JobProcessor.__init__()" |
| ta | \ref gen_proc.JobProcessor.timeAdvance "JobProcessor.timeAdvance()" |
| delta_int | \ref gen_proc.JobProcessor.intTransition "JobProcessor.intTransition()" |
| delta_ext | \ref gen_proc.JobProcessor.extTransition "JobProcessor.extTransition()" |
| delta_con | \ref gen_proc.JobProcessor.confTransition "JobProcessor.confTransition()" |
| lambda | \ref gen_proc.JobProcessor.outputFnc "JobProcessor.outputFnc()" |
*/
